     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me, and I'll add a note documenting that it was verified. You may also want to check it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
